Encryption vs Hashing — short practical view (developer perspective).

---

**1️⃣ Encryption (Reversible)**

* Data ko **secret form me convert** karta hai.
* **Decrypt karke original data wapas mil sakta hai.**
* Usually **key use hoti hai**.

**Common Use Cases**

* HTTPS
* Secure data storage
* API communication

**Example (Java – AES Encryption / Decryption)**

```java
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import java.util.Base64;

public class EncryptionExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {

        KeyGenerator keyGenerator = KeyGenerator.getInstance("AES");
        keyGenerator.init(128);
        SecretKey secretKey = keyGenerator.generateKey();

        String text = "prem123";

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES");

        // ENCRYPT
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, secretKey);
        byte[] encrypted = cipher.doFinal(text.getBytes());
        String encryptedText = Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(encrypted);

        System.out.println("Encrypted: " + encryptedText);

        // DECRYPT
        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, secretKey);
        byte[] decrypted = cipher.doFinal(Base64.getDecoder().decode(encryptedText));

        System.out.println("Decrypted: " + new String(decrypted));
    }
}
```

---

**2️⃣ Hashing (One-way / Irreversible)**

* Data ko **fixed-length hash value** me convert karta hai.
* **Original data wapas nahi mil sakta.**
* Mainly **password verification** ke liye.

**Common Use Cases**

* Password storage
* Data integrity
* Digital signatures

**Example (Java – SHA-256 Hash)**

```java
import java.security.MessageDigest;

public class HashExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {

        String password = "prem123";

        MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");

        byte[] hashBytes = md.digest(password.getBytes());

        StringBuilder hex = new StringBuilder();

        for (byte b : hashBytes) {
            hex.append(String.format("%02x", b));
        }

        System.out.println("Hash: " + hex);
    }
}
```

---

**3️⃣ Quick Interview Table**

| Feature       | Encryption             | Hashing              |
| ------------- | ---------------------- | -------------------- |
| Reversible    | Yes (decrypt possible) | No                   |
| Purpose       | Secure communication   | Password storage     |
| Key Required  | Yes                    | No                   |
| Output Length | Variable               | Fixed                |
| Examples      | AES, RSA               | SHA-256, MD5, bcrypt |

---

**4️⃣ Real Production Example**

Password storage (Spring Security style)

```java
import org.springframework.security.crypto.bcrypt.BCryptPasswordEncoder;

public class PasswordHash {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        BCryptPasswordEncoder encoder = new BCryptPasswordEncoder();

        String rawPassword = "prem123";

        String hash = encoder.encode(rawPassword);

        boolean match = encoder.matches("prem123", hash);

        System.out.println(hash);
        System.out.println(match);
    }
}
```

